WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.000
GENESIS: JURIS Studio — from a short brief to a playable and explainable legal scenario.

00:00:05.000 --> 00:00:14.000
Studio opens in User View. Technical identifiers stay out of the way while the complete professional workflow remains available.

00:00:14.000 --> 00:00:27.000
Paste the situation in the form experts actually receive it. Five concise lines define the parties, urgency, evidence problem, financial offer and decision.

00:00:27.000 --> 00:00:42.000
AI does not silently build or publish. It produces a read-only candidate scheme, exposing every proposed node, relation, deadline, consequence, assumption and economic input.

00:00:42.000 --> 00:00:57.000
Apply the reviewed proposal as one atomic revision. Select one node and refine its title, facts, timing, budget or professional consequence directly in the editor.

00:00:57.000 --> 00:01:15.000
Relationships remain under human control. Add a route, relink its source or destination, delete the exact connection and undo the complete change without losing version history.

00:01:15.000 --> 00:01:35.000
Launch the validated graph in the same player used by published cases. Decisions advance time, expose evidence, consume budget and workload, and lead to authored consequences.

00:01:35.000 --> 00:01:45.000
The final ledger keeps economics explicit: EUR 64,500 settlement, EUR 2,350 spend and EUR 62,150 net result.

00:01:45.000 --> 00:01:54.000
More Actions exposes the portable Final case prompt in Markdown. PDF export contains the summary, economics, sources, verification checklist, graph, node conditions and fingerprint.

00:01:54.000 --> 00:02:00.000
AI proposes. Professionals decide. The case remains deterministic, reviewable and ready to improve.
